Points $A,B,C$ lie on a circle. Let $P$ be the intersection of the tangents to the circle at $B$ and $C$. Lines $AB$ and $CP$ are parallel, and $AB=3$, $BP=4$. Find the length of segment $BC$. Here $XY$ denotes the length of segment $XY$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(280);
pair B=(0,-1),P=(2,-1),C=(0.8,0.6),A=(-0.96,0.28);
draw(unitcircle);draw(A--B--C--P--B);
label("A",A,(-1,1));label("B",B,(0,-1));label("C",C,(1,1));label("P",P,(1,-1));
[/asy]

Let $n\ge2$ be an integer. A regular hexagon $ABCDEF$ of side length $n$ is subdivided into equilateral triangles of side length $1$, as in the left-hand figure. Call the vertices of these equilateral triangles vertices.

A piece is initially at the center of hexagon $ABCDEF$. At each vertex $P$ strictly inside the hexagon, arrows point from $P$ toward four of the six vertices joined to $P$ by an edge of length $1$, as illustrated in the right-hand figure. When the piece is at $P$, it may be moved to any of these four vertices. For an edge $PQ$ of length $1$, the ability to move from $P$ to $Q$ does not necessarily imply the ability to move from $Q$ to $P$.

Prove that there is an integer $k$ such that, however the arrows are drawn, the piece can reach a vertex on the boundary of hexagon $ABCDEF$ in at most $k$ moves. Find the smallest possible value of $k$.

[asy]
import geometry;
settings.tex="none";
defaultpen(black+linewidth(0.65));
size(610);
real rt=sqrt(3)/2;int n=5;
pair[] V;for(int k=0;k<6;++k)V.push(n*dir(120+60*k));
path hex=V[0];for(int k=1;k<6;++k)hex=hex--V[k];hex=hex--cycle;
picture grid;
for(int j=-2*n;j<=2*n;++j){
 draw(grid,(-2*n,j*rt)--(2*n,j*rt),gray(0.5)+linewidth(0.35));
 draw(grid,(-n+j,-2*n*rt)--(n+j,2*n*rt),gray(0.5)+linewidth(0.35));
 draw(grid,(-n+j,2*n*rt)--(n+j,-2*n*rt),gray(0.5)+linewidth(0.35));
}
clip(grid,hex);add(grid);draw(hex);
string[] names={"A","B","C","D","E","F"};
for(int k=0;k<6;++k)label(names[k],V[k],unit(V[k]));dot((0,0));
label("(a)",(0,-n*rt-0.75));
pair shift=(13,0);
pair[] centers={shift+(0,1.8),shift+(-1.55,-0.9),shift+(1.55,-0.9)};
for(int k=0;k<3;++k){pair c=centers[k];for(int j=0;j<3;++j){pair d=dir(60*j);draw((c-1.45*d)--(c+1.45*d),gray(0.5)+linewidth(0.4));}
 int[] dirs={0,180,120,240};
 if(k==1)dirs=new int[]{0,180,60,240};
 if(k==2)dirs=new int[]{0,180,60,240};
 for(int a:dirs)draw(c--(c+0.95*dir(a)),black+linewidth(0.9),Arrow(5));
}
label("(b)",shift+(0,-n*rt-0.75));
[/asy]
